he things  that clogs your pores sometimes your  body is just not a team player one of  the big components of sebum is guayline  which is also a skincare ingredient this  reacts with oxygen and in light and it  goes from runny to sticky and more solid  so this starts sticking dead skin cells  together to form little plugs in your  skin that clog your pores and these are  called microcomedones so cleansing  reduces the amount of sebum on your face  and gets rid of some of the stuff that's  already reacted and so that helps to  reduce clogged pores another good reason  to use a cleansing is really just the  feel cleansers get dirt and oil off your  skin as well as any skincare or makeup  products that you're using i talk a lot  more about choosing and using a good  cleanser in my ebook the lab muffin  guide to basic skin get but in short  stripping your skin with cleansing is  not a good approach you can't just bully  your skin into behaving it makes oily  skin feel worse and it irritates your  skin if you have acne prone skin that's  even worse because irritation is one of  the factors that contributes to acne  along with oil and lots of dead skin  cells which i mentioned before cleanses  with high ph can also disturb your skin  and make it easier for acne bacteria to  spread and really get ingrained into  your skin anyway i think a lot of people  especially people who are new to skin  care tend to underestimate how important  a good cleanser is because they wash off  so it seems like it doesn't have that  much of an impact it's only on your skin  for a short amount of time  but in reality a good cleanser can make  a massive difference so here are my  picks for budget friendly cleanses that  work well for acne prone skin a  disclaimer this video isn't sponsored  but i've been sponsored by some of these  brands in the past and i was sent  samples of a lot of these products but  these are my genuine recommendations i  really like the bioderma cleansing gels  they come 